WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Heat blurs a hidden A. Three models use the same noisy temperature measurements.
One compact model learns from letters (including A); another learns from circles.

00:06.000 --> 00:17.000
Recorded optimization steps: full model, 961 values; letter-trained POD, 14;
circle-trained POD, 13. Dashed outlines are the reference; solid outlines are recovered.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.000
Both compact models have finished. Compare their shapes.
The remaining replay will now accelerate tenfold.

00:19.000 --> 00:25.500
The full model continues at 10 times the opening playback rate.
On-screen clocks still report the original measured compute time.

00:25.500 --> 00:30.000
Full model: 5.56 s, 92% shape overlap. Letter-trained POD: 48 ms, 84% overlap.
Circle-trained POD: 56 ms, 55% overlap.

00:30.000 --> 00:34.000
The letter-trained model is about 116 times faster in this iterative benchmark.
A was included in training. Timings exclude offline training; direct solves are faster here.
